Reading the later sections yielded a stronger, paper-internal justification than the preliminary leftover-hash argument: Section 6, Proposition 6.1 defines exactly the challenge “sample coefficients and a uniform binary input, publish the spherical-function output, recover any preimage” and proves this is a one-way family under the same SIVP assumption. I’m aligning the generator to that exact distribution—uniform bits, not fixed weight—and strengthening the LLL attack to guess several likely Hamming weights.
