+"""Generator/verifier for arXiv:2405.03591.
+
+The paper identifies a one-to-one correspondence between constrained
+inhomogeneous spherical equations over
+
+    G_(p,n) = F_p^n semidirect_product F_p^*
+
+and binary inhomogeneous short-integer-solution (ISIS) instances.  This module
+inverse-generates the native group equations: it chooses a binary witness first,
+samples all group coefficients independently and uniformly, and derives the
+right-hand side.  Verification is exact modular group arithmetic.
+
+The planted witness is sampled uniformly at weight m/2.  Since the maps
+x -> A x form a universal hash family, the planted public instance is within
+1/2*sqrt(p^n / binomial(m,m/2)) statistical distance of the paper's uniform
+instance distribution.  The default asymptotic schedule makes this negligible.
+"""
