codex
The concurrent builder has finished. Its Track B construction is mathematically sound: alternating scalar parts make the total scalar product \(1\), while the prefix-weighted vector parts telescope to \((t^m-1)v\); one sparse conjugator cancels that endpoint exactly. Literal group multiplication passes on demos, and the disclosed Section 4.1 reference algorithm succeeds 8/8 at about 1.31 million modular operations. The external oracle key is currently returning HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded,” so I will preserve that as infrastructure failure and will not report fabricated oracle attempts.
