Implemented a self-contained Track B generator based on the paper’s native semidirect-product spherical equations.

Key results:

- G1–G9(c) local gates pass.
- Shipping preset: 262,144 coefficients.
- Reference algorithm: 1,310,761 modular operations, about 1.20 seconds.
- Compact telescoping route: at most 70 measured operations.
- Guess density: exactly `1/(2^61-1)`; 0/200,000 sampled hits.
- Four adversarial attacks failed across 8/8 seeds.
- Answer: 44 characters worst case and 2 atomic elements.

Files:

- [Generator](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2405.03591/gen_2405_03591.py)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2405.03591/selftest_report.json)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2405.03591/README.md)
- [Bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2405.03591/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2405.03591/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2405.03591/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

The remaining blocker is external: every OpenRouter request returned HTTP 403, “Key limit exceeded (total limit).” Consequently, no valid Step 4 or G9 oracle attempt occurred, and the module cannot honestly be declared hardened yet. The error transcripts are preserved and no API failure was counted as a model failure.

After restoring OpenRouter quota, rerun from this directory:

```bash
python3 ../../scripts/harden.py gen_2405_03591.py
```

The paper was not rejected: Section 4.1 supports this Track B construction, while Section 5’s uniform constrained-instance theorem does not justify a Track A claim for planted instances. [Full paper](https://arxiv.org/html/2405.03591v2).
